6. Crucial Architectural Considerations & Enhancements
* Webhook Reliability vs Direct Redirection:
Never rely solely on client-side redirect query strings to unlock theme editing access. Webhook verification ensures payment confirmation even if the user closes their browser window during redirection.
* Free vs Paid Themes Handling:
If theme.price === 0, skip payment gateway completely and directly initialize the editor workspace via a POST /api/v1/portfolios/initialize route.
* Auto-Saving in Editor:
Implement debounced auto-save (e.g., 2000ms delay) on the Next.js frontend using RTK Query/Axios to sync local JSON state seamlessly back to MongoDB.
* Security & Ownership Checks:
Implement middleware on express server (verifyThemeOwnership) to prevent unauthorized editing of premium themes unless a verified completed purchase record exists in purchases collection.


