7. Sidebar Inspector & Property Panel Architecture (Webflow-Style Editor Layout)
1. Workspace & Editor UI Layout
   * Top Control Bar:
Displays overall workspace controls including theme switcher, device viewport toggles (Desktop, Tablet, Mobile), undo/redo actions, auto-save status indicators, live preview link, and the primary "Publish" button.
   * Left Main Canvas Area:
Renders the interactive WYSIWYG portfolio preview inside an isolated iframe or virtual canvas shell. Component elements render selection borders, hover highlights, and drag handles corresponding to the dynamic JSON node tree.
   * Right Property Panel (Style & Content Inspector):
Context-aware sidebar panel inspired by Webflow/Framer. When an element on the canvas is selected, the inspector dynamically populates corresponding tabs for styling (Typography, Color, Spacing, Layout) and content editing (Text fields, Image uploads, Link targets).
2. React State Management & Inspector Sync Architecture
      * Node Selection Flow:
Clicking any editable element on the canvas updates the global editor state (e.g., setting selectedNodeId via Redux Toolkit / Zustand).
      * Dynamic Controls Rendering:
The right property panel reads selectedNodeId from state, extracts the node's schema properties, and dynamically renders dedicated UI form controls:
         * Typography & Color: Font family dropdowns, font weight, size sliders, color pickers, and alignment controls.
         * Spacing & Layout: Interactive margin/padding visual box model, flex/grid properties, width/height dimensions.
         * Backgrounds & Borders: Fill colors, image overlays, border radius, and box shadows.
         * Content Fields: Direct text input controls, asset managers for images, and URL link destination pickers.
         * Real-Time Tree Updates & Persistence:
Input adjustments in the inspector trigger targeted state dispatches (e.g., updateNodeStyle({ nodeId, path, value })), mutating the core JSON document structure instantly in memory to reflect real-time updates on the canvas. State changes trigger a debounced persistence service (2000ms delay) that sends a POST /api/v1/portfolios/save payload back to MongoDB.